WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
- Let's get to our first guest,

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.610
even in the crazy year of 2020,

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.530
she's been as busy as ever.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:08.480
You can catch her in
Space Force on Netflix

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.110
and in her Emmy winning role on

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.550
The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel on Amazon.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:13.470
Plus, this summer,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.080
she's back with the new season
of Hollywood Game Night.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.270
I love Hollywood Game Night.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.182
Take a look.

00:00:18.182 --> 00:00:20.740
- Everybody focus, and
here is our first dance.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:21.573
Go!

00:00:22.518 --> 00:00:24.796
(audience laughter)

00:00:24.796 --> 00:00:25.629
- Vogueing.

00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:27.546
- That's right, Vogue.

00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:29.900
- What were you doing?

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.140
What is happening to me?

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.490
- [Player] Breakdancing!

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.323
- Limbo!

00:00:33.323 --> 00:00:35.238
- [Jane] That is right.

00:00:37.752 --> 00:00:39.360
(audience cheers)

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.212
- Twerking.

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:41.904
- [Jane] Twerking.

00:00:41.904 --> 00:00:43.179
- Miss Jane Lynch,

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:44.840
Hello, can you hear me?

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.350
- There's Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.240
- Oh, hi Jane.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.081
Hi!

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.853
How are you?

00:00:49.853 --> 00:00:50.987
- I'm well, how are you?

00:00:50.987 --> 00:00:54.060
- I'm well, I think we're,
you know, all, you know,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.959
every day is like, okay.

00:00:55.959 --> 00:00:57.547
That's what I feel like every day is.

00:00:57.547 --> 00:00:59.254
- Absolutely.

00:00:59.254 --> 00:01:01.980
- Hey, you know how much I
love Hollywood Game Night,

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.920
probably more than I should,

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.700
cause I'm annoying when I play games.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.940
But is anyone there?

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.360
This is a real question.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.193
- Yes.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:11.099
- Is anyone as competitive
as me this season?

00:01:11.099 --> 00:01:12.100
- Yes.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.510
But there's a difference
between the two of you.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.702
And I will tell you what that is.

00:01:15.702 --> 00:01:20.130
Yvette Nicole Brown is
extremely competitive,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.870
but unlike you, Kelly,

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.470
she's stealthy.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.303
- Oh.

00:01:24.303 --> 00:01:25.220
She's sneaky about it.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:26.053
You are obvious.

00:01:26.053 --> 00:01:27.990
That's the word.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.550
You're obvious and you're transparent

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.150
and delightful and charming.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.803
Whereas she just kind
of sits back and goes,

00:01:32.803 --> 00:01:33.720
pew,

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.070
like a Scorpio, you know,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.780
she comes like out of
the depth of the ocean

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.390
and goes and bites you.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.281
- Yeah.

00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:40.114
And you're like, what just happened?

00:01:40.114 --> 00:01:41.051
- Exactly.

00:01:41.051 --> 00:01:42.456
- I wish I were more like a ninja,

00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:44.314
but I'm still obvious.

00:01:44.314 --> 00:01:45.883
- You gotta be Kelly.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.440
- I love, I love the game night.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.620
You did you did a special episode though,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.080
from your house, looking
into other celebrities homes,

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.590
which I thought was kind of cool,

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.660
whose house made you most jealous?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.372
- I loved my house the best.

00:02:00.372 --> 00:02:01.205
- I love it!

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:04.267
- It's confirmed my design
choices in my partner

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.150
who's really good at this too,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.117
but I mean everybody's house,

00:02:07.117 --> 00:02:09.210
you couldn't see theirs as much as ours,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.280
but we had these really great steps,

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.784
like kind of architecturally,

00:02:12.784 --> 00:02:15.640
that I'd never saw before this way.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.131
And I was so thrilled with how we,

00:02:18.131 --> 00:02:20.710
how we had the books and the shelves

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:21.543
and you know,

00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:23.360
we kind of styled it and
we kept it that way too.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.896
Cause it was kind of a mess
with a bunch of family pictures

00:02:25.896 --> 00:02:28.150
and we made some edits.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.176
We got rid of some family members, sorry,

00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:33.870
we just made a really beautiful display.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.360
And we kept it that way.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.193
- That's awesome.

00:02:36.193 --> 00:02:37.026
I love that answer too,

00:02:37.026 --> 00:02:39.190
because I feel like we always
want what we don't have

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:40.023
and that's nice.

00:02:40.023 --> 00:02:42.035
It's such a lovely thing to like, go,

00:02:42.035 --> 00:02:44.840
"No, I like my home."

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:45.900
- I like yours too.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.540
I don't know where you
are, but it looks great.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.481
And it's beautiful.

00:02:48.481 --> 00:02:49.314
- This is not--

00:02:49.314 --> 00:02:50.147
I mean we're in my home,

00:02:50.147 --> 00:02:52.450
but this is literally a set that,

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.283
they came,

00:02:53.283 --> 00:02:55.390
like it was only allowed
like one person with a mask.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.955
Like, I mean, this is literally,

00:02:56.955 --> 00:02:59.040
it's an actual set in my living room

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.072
so my house doesn't normally
have my initials everywhere.

00:03:03.072 --> 00:03:04.320
- I was gonna say.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.293
- Not much of a tool, Jane.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.090
- I got a big JL over there.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.490
You just don't see it.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.323
- That's awesome.

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:12.632
So Jane, we have the pandemic,

00:03:12.632 --> 00:03:15.782
we have the black lives matter movement.

00:03:15.782 --> 00:03:17.350
There's just a lot of change.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.183
And I, you know,

00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:20.610
I think that if we do it right,

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.200
it's a change in a great direction.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.086
And I feel like it's been needing
to happen for generations.

00:03:25.086 --> 00:03:29.400
But I was just curious how you
were processing everything.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.250
- Well, you know,

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.540
there's this thing called Twitter

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.200
and it's a double edged sword.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.033
- Amen.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.970
- I've never laughed harder

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.750
than when I go through my Twitter feed.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.131
I've never felt as heartbroken

00:03:41.131 --> 00:03:43.560
than when I go through my Twitter feed.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.550
I've never been as angry,
and that's the worst part.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.860
So it's kind of a, that's
where I get my news.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.980
It's been a bit of an addiction for me

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.300
and I'm suffering a little bit over it.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.571
So I'm not sure where to put it,

00:03:57.571 --> 00:03:59.140
you know,

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.766
there is just so much going on
and I feel like I got to know

00:04:02.766 --> 00:04:05.630
what it is and I've got to
understand it, you know?

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.250
And I think that that's a healthy thing

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.470
because we are at a tipping point.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.303
This is,

00:04:09.303 --> 00:04:13.210
this is a really tender
moment in our history

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.043
and our

00:04:14.043 --> 00:04:16.980
nation's history, you know,

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.020
are we going to survive this?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.287
You know,

00:04:20.287 --> 00:04:21.620
the institutions and,

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.190
are we going to tear each other apart?

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.023
I mean,

00:04:24.023 --> 00:04:26.930
we're really, we're
really at a tipping point.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.763
- [Kelly] I agree.

00:04:27.763 --> 00:04:28.596
I agree.

00:04:28.596 --> 00:04:29.515
Speaking of social change,

00:04:29.515 --> 00:04:31.006
The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel

00:04:31.006 --> 00:04:32.927
deals with a lot of
social change on the show.

00:04:32.927 --> 00:04:37.927
How do you think the period of
that show reminds you of now?

00:04:38.042 --> 00:04:39.920
- Well, it's in the early sixties,

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.920
so we wouldn't have the 68, 69 stuff,

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.155
the horrible assassinations
for a few years,

00:04:48.155 --> 00:04:51.210
but it is very white dominated.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.280
It is very male dominated

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.440
and, kind of like today,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.440
and the women, like women today,

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.830
are trying to make their mark in comedy

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.070
and Midge Maisel is one of those pioneers

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.243
because she doesn't,

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.090
she doesn't agree with
the power structure.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.520
She doesn't even, you know,
she reminds me of a way of,

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.777
in a way of Tina Fey and Amy Poehler,

00:05:13.777 --> 00:05:15.820
who kind of just took a seat at the table

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:16.750
without being invited,

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.930
just they're entitled to it.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.540
And I think that's who Midge Maisel is

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.260
and my character, Sophie Lennon,
is more of the old school.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.240
You know,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.580
you have to act in a certain way,

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.320
you have to make fun of your looks,

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.650
you have to say you're fat,

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.490
everything has to revolve around,

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:34.310
the comedy has to revolve
around how you can't get a date

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.104
or you can't get a
husband to stay with you

00:05:36.104 --> 00:05:38.827
and, you know, Midge
is stepping up, going,

00:05:38.827 --> 00:05:40.219
"That's not funny,"

00:05:40.219 --> 00:05:41.290
you know?

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.123
And I say to her,

00:05:42.123 --> 00:05:42.956
"Well, what's your gimmick?"

00:05:42.956 --> 00:05:43.789
She says,

00:05:43.789 --> 00:05:44.622
"I don't have a gimmick."

00:05:44.622 --> 00:05:45.890
"I just, you know, I tell funny stories."

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.270
So, you know, very much like today.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:49.103
- Yeah.

00:05:49.103 --> 00:05:51.430
I mean, it's super sad in one aspect,

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.553
but also, like, super telling.

